## Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes

Each entry in `entitlements` is populated by the same conversion code as the
singular [`identitynow_entitlement_v1` data source](../data-sources/entitlement_v1.md) -
see the [`identitynow_entitlement_v1` resource](../resources/entitlement_v1.md)'s
"Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes" section for details on `attributes`,
`manually_updated_fields`, and `access_model_metadata`.

The API's documented maximum `limit` for `GET /entitlements/v1` is 250;
requested limits above that are capped with a warning rather than an error.

### Eventual consistency after source aggregation

Entitlements only exist once a source aggregation has imported them. Because
Terraform data sources are read exactly once per plan/apply with no built-in
retry/backoff, reading this data source too soon after triggering an
aggregation (e.g. via the future `identitynow_source_load_entitlement_wait_v1`
helper resource) can return fewer entitlements than expected. See
`examples/data-sources/identitynow_entitlements_v1/data-source.tf` for the
recommended `depends_on`-based ordering and an optional `lifecycle.postcondition`
guard against silently under-provisioning from an incomplete result.
